{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "notes": [
    "Paired scenario fixtures. Every scenario belongs to exactly one PAIR, and the",
    "pair declares the ONE dimension it varies (`variantAxis`). The runner enforces",
    "that: a pair whose members differ in anything else fails BEFORE check.mjs is",
    "invoked, because a difference in the advice would then prove nothing.",
    "",
    "  variantAxis   members must share                      members must vary",
    "  -----------   --------------------------------------  -----------------",
    "  target        source, map, style, gain, mode, roles    target",
    "  style         source, target, map, mode, roles         style",
    "  map           source, target, style, gain, mode, roles map",
    "  roles         source, target, map, style, gain         lead/rhythm",
    "  configuration source, target, map, style               any other run flag",
    "",
    "`polarity` says what the pair member CLAIMS: `positive` = the toolchain should",
    "stay quiet about the thing under test, `negative` = it should speak,",
    "`comparison` = neither, this member exists to be diffed. Every pair needs at",
    "least one positive and at least one non-positive.",
    "",
    "Expectations are advisory CODES, never prose (C3), so wording stays free to",
    "improve. `forbiddenAdvisoryCodes` is the half that earns its keep: it is where",
    "a false positive gets caught.",
    "",
    "`map: null` means BAR-LOCKED (no --map) and must be written explicitly — an",
    "omitted key is a schema error, so 'I forgot the map' can never read as 'I meant",
    "bar-locked'.",
    "",
    "Paths are relative to tools/fixtures/. The runner is tools/lib/scenarios.test.mjs.",
    "The coverage ledger is docs/specs/wave6-advisory-coverage.md."
  ],
  "scenarios": [
